{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And Moses spoke to the heads of the tribes.</b> What [does it mean that] he spoke to the heads of the tribes of the children of Israel, saying? He spoke to the heads of the tribes that they should say some matter to the children of Israel, and it did not yet specify what the heads of the tribes should say to the children of Israel, until he told them the passage of vows — that the head of the tribe is obligated to say to the one who vows, 'It is permitted to you.' And this is the saying that he commanded the heads of the tribes, that they should say to the children of Israel; and concerning this he said: 'He shall not break his word' — he himself shall not break it, but others may annul his word. And concerning this he said: 'according to all that proceeds from his mouth' — that is, from the mouth of the sage who permits it, thus 'he shall do' — whether to uphold or to annul."], :book :numbers, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:43:22.399771071Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}